    "Free-form structured config (provider-specific). `configuration.authentication` MAY carry a `credentialRef` object: `{\"credentialId\": \"<uuid>\"}` (primary) or `{\"credentialName\": \"<name>\"}` (convenience). To dispatch this source's calls in-process through the OpenRegister credential broker instead of embedding secrets. When `credentialRef` is present: any sibling field under `authentication` is a hard 409 config error at call time (embedded secrets are FORBIDDEN, never merged); setting both `credentialId` and `credentialName`, or an empty value, is a 409; an ambiguous `credentialName` (0 or >1 owned matches) is a 409; SOAP sources, asynchronous dispatch, and `cert`/`ssl_key` config are rejected in v1. The provider catalogue's host-lock is the sole authority for the target host. `location` remains configuration documentation. `configuration.decompress: \"gzip\"` hints that the fetched body is a gzip-compressed file (also auto-detected from a `.gz`-suffixed endpoint or an `application/gzip` response Content-Type). Gunzipped before the existing JSON/XML/JSONL parse attempts; `.tar.gz`/`.tar` archives are detected but NOT supported (logged + skipped). `configuration.listMethod`/`configuration.body` (pre-existing, see decideMethod/mergeSourceConfiguration) let a source declare a static POST body template. See `sourceConfig.paginationIn` below for advancing it across pages (change post-body-pagination)." : "Free-form structured config (provider-specific). `configuration.authentication` MAY carry a `credentialRef` object: `{\"credentialId\": \"<uuid>\"}` (primary) or `{\"credentialName\": \"<name>\"}` (convenience). To dispatch this source's calls in-process through the OpenRegister credential broker instead of embedding secrets. When `credentialRef` is present: any sibling field under `authentication` is a hard 409 config error at call time (embedded secrets are FORBIDDEN, never merged); setting both `credentialId` and `credentialName`, or an empty value, is a 409; an ambiguous `credentialName` (0 or >1 owned matches) is a 409; SOAP sources, asynchronous dispatch, and `cert`/`ssl_key` config are rejected in v1. The provider catalogue's host-lock is the sole authority for the target host. `location` remains configuration documentation. `configuration.decompress: \"gzip\"` hints that the fetched body is a gzip-compressed file (also auto-detected from a `.gz`-suffixed endpoint or an `application/gzip` response Content-Type). Gunzipped before the existing JSON/XML/JSONL parse attempts; `.tar.gz`/`.tar` archives are detected but NOT supported (logged + skipped). `configuration.listMethod`/`configuration.body` (pre-existing, see decideMethod/mergeSourceConfiguration) let a source declare a static POST body template. See `sourceConfig.paginationIn` below for advancing it across pages (change post-body-pagination).",
